# DataWeave Script Standards

## Externalization
- **All DataWeave scripts must be externalized** into `.dwl` files under `src/main/resources/dwls/`
- Inline DataWeave in Mule XML should be avoided — extract to external files
- Only trivial single-line expressions (e.g., `vars.httpStatus`) may remain inline

## File Naming
- Files must use **lower-case-hyphenated** format with `.dwl` extension
- Names must be concise and describe the transformation being performed
- Examples:
  - `create-issue-response-json.dwl`
  - `usps-api-parameters.dwl`
  - `p-set-common-error-response.dwl`

## Prefix Convention (from project patterns)
## - `v-` prefix: scripts that set variables (e.g., `v-request-context.dwl`)
## - `p-` prefix: scripts that set payload (e.g., `p-set-liveness-response.dwl`)
## - Follow existing prefix conventions consistently

## Error Mapping Scripts
- Custom error mapping DWL files go under `src/main/resources/errors/`
- Must map error types to appropriate HTTP status codes, reasons, and messages

## Review Checklist
- [ ] No complex inline DataWeave in Mule XML files
- [ ] DWL files are in `src/main/resources/dwls/` (or `errors/` for error maps)
- [ ] File names are lower-case-hyphenated and descriptive
## - [ ] Prefix convention (`v-`, `p-`) is followed consistently
